I was provided with a receipt and duly and officially accepted as an
      excursionist. There was happiness in that but it was tame compared to the
      novelty of being &ldquo;select.&rdquo;

I thought so. I anticipated him, anyhow. I stayed there and was bombarded
      with old gentlemen for an hour, perhaps; and all I got out of any of them
      was &ldquo;Oh, my!&rdquo;

&ldquo;Now, say&mdash;my friend&mdash;don&rsquo;t you know any better than to be
      whittling the ship all to pieces that way? You ought to know better than
      that.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Come, now, George, don&rsquo;t improvise. It looks too egotistical. It will
      provoke remark. Just stick to &lsquo;Coronation,&rsquo; like the others. It is a good
      tune&mdash;you can&rsquo;t improve it any, just off-hand, in this way.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Landlord, this is a low, mean swindle, and I&rsquo;ll never, never stand it.
      Here&rsquo;s a hundred and fifty dollars, Sir, and it&rsquo;s all you&rsquo;ll get&mdash;I&rsquo;ll
      swim in blood before I&rsquo;ll pay a cent more.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Do you see that there hill out there on that African coast? It&rsquo;s one of
      them Pillows of Herkewls, I should say&mdash;and there&rsquo;s the ultimate one
      alongside of it.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Oh, that will do&mdash;that&rsquo;s enough. If you have got your hand in for
      inventing authors and testimony, I have nothing more to say&mdash;let them
      be on the same side.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Well, yes, it is a little remarkable&mdash;singular tunnel altogether&mdash;stands
      up out of the top of the hill about two hundred feet, and one end of it
      sticks out of the hill about nine hundred!&rdquo;

&ldquo;This one does very well; it fits elegantly. I like a glove that fits. No,
      never mind, ma&rsquo;am, never mind; I&rsquo;ll put the other on in the street. It is
      warm here.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Yes, indeed, I&rsquo;ve noticed that when a man hauls on a kid glove like he
      was dragging a cat out of an ash hole by the tail, he understands putting
      on kid gloves; he&rsquo;s had ex&mdash;&rdquo;

&ldquo;Boys, enough of a thing&rsquo;s enough! You think you are very smart, I
      suppose, but I don&rsquo;t. And if you go and tell any of those old gossips in
      the ship about this thing, I&rsquo;ll never forgive you for it; that&rsquo;s all.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Oh, yes, it&rsquo;s all very well to say go to bed when a man makes an argument
      which another man can&rsquo;t answer. Dan don&rsquo;t never stand any chance in an
      argument with me. And he knows it, too. What should you say, Jack?&rdquo;

&ldquo;Well, go on, go on,&rdquo; he said, &ldquo;don&rsquo;t mind me. I don&rsquo;t wish to interfere.
      Only, if you go on telling him in your kind of French, he never will find
      out where we want to go to. That is what I think about it.&rdquo;

&ldquo;There now, Dan, he says he is going to allez to the douain. Means he is
      going to the hotel. Oh, certainly&mdash;we don&rsquo;t know the French
      language.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Doctor, there is a flaw in your pronunciation somewhere. Let me try her.
      Madame, avez-vous du vin?&mdash;It isn&rsquo;t any use, Doctor&mdash;take the
      witness.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Madame, avez-vous du vin&mdash;du fromage&mdash;pain&mdash;pickled pigs&rsquo;
      feet&mdash;beurre&mdash;des oeufs&mdash;du boeuf&mdash;horseradish,
      sauerkraut, hog and hominy&mdash;anything, anything in the world that can
      stay a Christian stomach!&rdquo;

&ldquo;Well, I wish they were educated enough to tell a man a direction that
      goes some where&mdash;for we&rsquo;ve been going around in a circle for an hour.
      I&rsquo;ve passed this same old drugstore seven times.&rdquo;

&ldquo;If ze zhentlemans will to me make ze grande honneur to me rattain in hees
      serveece, I shall show to him every sing zat is magnifique to look upon in
      ze beautiful Parree. I speaky ze Angleesh pairfaitemaw.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Beware, woman! Go away from here&mdash;go away, now, or it will be the
      worse for you. I am an unprotected male, but I will preserve my honor at
      the peril of my life!&rdquo;

&ldquo;Soap, you know&mdash;soap. That is what I want&mdash;soap. S-o-a-p, soap;
      s-o-p-e, soap; s-o-u-p, soap. Hurry up! I don&rsquo;t know how you Irish spell
      it, but I want it. Spell it to suit yourself, but fetch it. I&rsquo;m freezing.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Ah, that wonderful face is so humble, so pleading&mdash;it says as
      plainly as words could say it: &lsquo;I fear; I tremble; I am unworthy. But Thy
      will be done; sustain Thou Thy servant!&rsquo;&rdquo;

&ldquo;Well,&rdquo; he said; &ldquo;there is a legend connected with that iron hook. Nearly
      seven hundred years ago, that castle was the property of the noble Count
      Luigi Gennaro Guido Alphonso di Genova----&rdquo;

&ldquo;Marry,&rdquo; quoth the peasant, &ldquo;an&rsquo; it please your worships, ye had better
      journey many a good rood hence with your juggling circus than trust your
      bones in yonder castle.&rdquo;

&ldquo;&rsquo;Tis well. Dispose of them in the customary manner. Yet stay! I have need
      of them. Let them come hither. Later, cast them from the
      battlements--or--how many priests have ye on hand?&rdquo;

&ldquo;Meet me on the Tarpeian Rock tomorrow evening, dear, at sharp seven.
      Mother will be absent on a visit to her friends in the Sabine Hills.
      CLAUDIA.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Come wis me, genteelmen!--come! I show you ze letter writing by
      Christopher Colombo!--write it himself!--write it wis his own
      hand!--come!&rdquo;

&ldquo;Discover America. No--that statement will hardly wash. We are just from
      America ourselves. We heard nothing about it. Christopher
      Colombo--pleasant name--is--is he dead?&rdquo;

&ldquo;What do I want to see this place for? Young man, little do you know me,
      or you wouldn&rsquo;t ask such a question. I wish to see all the places that&rsquo;s
      mentioned in the Bible.&rdquo;

&ldquo;I perceive that I am pretty far gone. It is plain that I ought to be
      buried without any unnecessary delay. Perhaps you had better go after my
      friends at once, because the weather is warm, and I can not &lsquo;keep&rsquo; long.&rdquo;

In their pipes lingered no echo of the wonderful music the shepherd
      forefathers heard in the Plains of Bethlehem what time the angels sang
      &ldquo;Peace on earth, good will to men.&rdquo;

Another pilgrim came along presently and said: &ldquo;Observe that tall,
      graceful girl; what queenly Madonna-like gracefulness of beauty is in her
      countenance.&rdquo;

Samaria stood a disastrous siege, once, in the days of Elisha, at the
      hands of the King of Syria. Provisions reached such a figure that &ldquo;an ass&rsquo;
      head was sold for eighty pieces of silver and the fourth part of a cab of
      dove&rsquo;s dung for five pieces of silver.&rdquo;
